# Licensing

Three things apply here, depending on what you're looking at. All of them are
**noncommercial** — the difference is which instrument fits which material.

## Code → PolyForm Noncommercial 1.0.0

Full text: [LICENSE-code](LICENSE-code)

Compose files, shell scripts, tests, hooks — anything executable or
configuration.

Creative Commons explicitly recommend against using CC licences for software:
no patent grant, no source provisions, and "NonCommercial" is loosely defined
for code. PolyForm Noncommercial is the same posture, drafted for software.

## Documentation → CC BY-NC 4.0

Full text: [LICENSE-docs](LICENSE-docs)

Prose, guides, diagrams, README and everything under `docs/`. Creative Commons
is the right instrument for writing.

## Four files → CC BY-NC 4.0, pending permission

- `tests/e2e/networking.spec.ts`
- `tests/e2e/vpn-security.spec.ts`
- `tests/e2e/helpers.ts`
- `scripts/detect-vpn-zombies.sh`

These are adapted from [leonardoazeredo/ultimate-arr-stack](https://github.com/leonardoazeredo/ultimate-arr-stack),
a downstream fork, and were contributed to this project under CC BY-NC 4.0.
**They remain under CC BY-NC 4.0 until their author agrees to the change** —
relicensing someone else's copyright without asking is not ours to do. The
request is [issue #20](https://github.com/Pharkie/ultimate-arr-stack/issues/20).

`tests/e2e/helpers.ts` is a mixed file: only its docker-exec helpers derive
from that work. The whole file is offered under CC BY-NC 4.0 anyway, because
splitting a 106-line file by authorship would be worse for everyone reading it.

## Notes

**This change is forward-only.** Copies already distributed under CC BY-NC 4.0
— including every existing fork — keep those terms permanently. Nothing is
withdrawn from anyone.

**Contributors:** [@gncnpk](https://github.com/gncnpk) agreed to the relicence
on 2026-08-15 (issue #20). [@eren-kemer](https://github.com/eren-kemer)'s
contribution has no surviving lines, confirmed by `git blame`, so no agreement
was needed.

**GitHub will report this repository as unlicensed.** Its detector recognises
thirteen licences and includes neither PolyForm nor any NonCommercial CC
variant. That's cosmetic — these files are what have legal effect.

Individual software components deployed by this stack (Sonarr, Radarr,
Jellyfin, and the rest) retain their own licences, which have nothing to do
with this repository.
